# Copy to `.env.local`. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# Every variable is REQUIRED and has no default. src/server/config.ts validates them when the
# server starts, and `next dev` / `next start` exits naming each missing or malformed one and
# why, never its value. A variable set to nothing counts as missing.
#
# None of them is NEXT_PUBLIC_*: nothing here is inlined into the browser's bundle. A page gets
# the addresses it links to as props from the server. Every address is a setting, never a
# literal (ADR-0187 §7).

# APP_ENV — one of: local | development | staging | production
#
# The same four names the backend and the other apps use (docs/environments.md). **Only `local`
# runs today.** Outside `local`, PUBLIC_SITE_URL and both store links must be https://.
APP_ENV=local

# API_URL — the backend, called from this server and never from the browser. Server to server, so
# no scheme rule. The backend's dev stack answers here (backend/docker-compose-local.yml).
API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# PUBLIC_SITE_URL — this site's own address, as people reach it: the backend's own
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL, which every group link is printed under. The preview's image and address are
# absolute URLs made from it, so a messenger fetches from here. A domain is a deploy-time item.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# APP_STORE_URL and GOOGLE_PLAY_URL — where the store buttons go: Raketa's listings. No listing
# exists yet (a deploy-time item), so the App Store placeholder opens the store's own not-found
# page, and Google Play's names the app's package, which has no page until it is published.
APP_STORE_URL=https://apps.apple.com/app/raketa/id0000000000
GOOGLE_PLAY_URL=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.raketa.player

# APP_SCHEME — the player app's own scheme, without "://" (frontend_player's app.config.ts, and
# the backend's APP_SCHEME). Open in Raketa goes to <APP_SCHEME>://join/<code>. A web or script
# scheme is refused.
APP_SCHEME=raketa
